Unit Testing 
Unit testing is a testing technique whihc is used to test the smallest part of program independently and and automatically


Adaptability
1. Maintains the quality of program
2.Tests each funcionality
3. Main intention is to find the locical bugs in the program
4. Not time-consuming


Junit
Junit is the testing framework in java used to test the individula logic of program

Basic annotation in junit

@Test == Test Method
@BeforeAll -- indicates to apply before all the methods
@BeforeEach -- indicates to apply before each methods
@AfterEach -- indicates to apply after each methods
@AfterAll -- indeicates to apply after all methods
@DisplayName == Indicates name 
@Disabled == skips test  case
@Tag == Basically used to give the tags or names to the method

to print the tags we will require the instance of TestInfo testInfo 
then there is a method called testinfor.getTags();

Lifecycle order
BeforeAll 
BeforeEach
Test
AfterEach
AfterAll

Common Methods
1.AssertEquals -- check the value is matching or not
2. AssertTrue -- return true if the condition is true and passes the test case
3.AssertFalse -- return true if the condition is false
4. AssertsNull -- passes the test case if the value is null
5. AssertsNotNull -- passes if the value is not null


